From: pulipakaa24 <adipu@utexas.edu>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:08:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] METALSIM_CHANGES.md: EPA horizon fallbacks as MuJoCo C,
 shrink flag, import-time flags

---
 METALSIM_CHANGES.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/METALSIM_CHANGES.md b/METALSIM_CHANGES.md
index 2cbc2ab..b954049 100644
--- a/METALSIM_CHANGES.md
+++ b/METALSIM_CHANGES.md
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ The changes below modify Apache-2.0 code and are offered under the same licence.
 | `8227c3b` | `_solve_done` keeps the solver's iteration count in a local (it read back an in-place increment, which Warp's deterministic counting pass suppresses: a world at the iteration cap then made the early exit's counter call in one pass only); the counter's return is consumed only with the early exit. |
 | `bf2e209` | Warp's deterministic mode takes the unfused Newton update (the fused kernel reads back its own change counter within the launch; its deterministic plan at 1,024 worlds asked for more than 2^31 scratch elements). |
 | `d514112`, `bdc3f71`, `7f6310d`, tests | Heightfield contacts against the exact geometry (MetalSim `docs/research/hfield_contacts_2026-10-31.md`). (1) The prism is a plain convex polytope, as in MuJoCo C (`collision_gjk.HFIELD_PRISM_POLYTOPE`): upstream #928's side-wall override in `_inflate` / `_epa_witness` returned a vertical penetration for prisms clear of the geom (a 5 mm sphere 8.6 mm clear came back 25.6 mm deep). (2) The prism support returns vertex index 0-5: with -2 / -3 for all six vertices discrete EPA (box, mesh) stopped at a "repeated" vertex (a box 9.25 mm into a prism came back 2.57 mm; MuJoCo C's `mjc_prism_support` has the same defect). (3) `ccd_hfield_kernel`: penetrating prisms only; contacts 1-3 skip duplicates (1e-4 m and 0.05 deg, `HFIELD_SELECT_DEDUP`) instead of stopping within 1 mm, which lost a sphere's second face in a crease; prisms relative to the other geom (`HFIELD_LOCAL_ORIGIN`); margin and gap as MuJoCo C main 8626d3c (`HFIELD_TRUE_DISTANCE`). (4) Meshes take GJK/EPA (`HFIELD_PLANE_CONTACTS` now False; the plane path missed terrain vertices inside a mesh face: Isaac's G1 foot, no contact in 178 of 1000 touching placements); Warp's deterministic mode keeps the plane path for meshes. g1_bumps tile, against the exact sets: sphere contact sets 88.8 -> 99.97 %, box 76.6 -> 99.9 %, G1 foot mesh 52.9 -> 99.9 %, normals > 10 deg 6.1 / 16.9 / 9.5 % -> 0. Five `-k hfield` tests added. |
-| `439b808`, `f85879c` | EPA horizon and the heightfield margin (MetalSim `docs/research/hfield_contacts_2026-10-31.md` §12). (1) EPA's horizon scan tested every face on its own, so with the support point on (to rounding) the planes of several faces it deleted faces not connected to the closest face; the horizon was then not one loop and the fixed 24-edge buffer could fill, and EPA returned no face: the pair lost its contact (`EPA_HORIZON`; Isaac's G1 feet on the rough heightfield with Isaac Lab 3.0's geom gap, a few worlds per 4096-world PPO iteration). As MuJoCo C (`horizon` / `horizonRec`), the deleted region now grows from the closest face when the scan's horizon is not one loop (a scan that gives one loop is kept: bitwise unchanged); the buffer is sized `3 (5 + ccd_iterations) - 6` (`epa_horizon_size`); a full buffer or a region that is still not a disk ends EPA with its closest face instead of no contact, and so does a full face buffer (MuJoCo C's `epa`). (2) `HFIELD_MARGIN_SHRINK` (default True): a heightfield prism pair with a margin or gap runs GJK on the uninflated shapes first and EPA only when they overlap, as MuJoCo C's `mjc_ccd` (upstream does it for non-heightfield pairs); before, every prism within margin + gap ran EPA on the inflated shapes. No effect at margin = gap = 0 (heightfield contact checks bitwise unchanged). rough_il3 smoke (4096 envs, 8 iterations, the 14-inch on AC, ratios only): `EPA_HORIZON` 3 worlds -> 0; per PPO iteration 2.05x the plane-path pin `8eb51fe` -> 1.68x; the 2.3.2 heightfield config unchanged (+0.3 %). |
+| `439b808`, `f85879c`, `d7a90fb`, `3d8f48c`, tests | EPA horizon and the heightfield margin (MetalSim `docs/research/hfield_contacts_2026-10-31.md` §12). (1) EPA's horizon scan tested every face on its own, so with the support point on (to rounding) the planes of several faces it deleted faces not connected to the closest face; the horizon was then not one loop and the fixed 24-edge buffer could fill, and EPA returned no face: the pair lost its contact (`EPA_HORIZON`; Isaac's G1 feet on the rough heightfield with Isaac Lab 3.0's geom gap, a few worlds per 4096-world PPO iteration). As MuJoCo C (`horizon` / `horizonRec`), the deleted region now grows from the closest face when the scan's horizon is not one loop (a scan that gives one loop is kept: bitwise unchanged); the buffer is sized `3 (5 + ccd_iterations) - 6` (`epa_horizon_size`); a full buffer (`EPA_HORIZON`) or a region that is still not a disk returns no contact, as MuJoCo C's `epa` when its horizon runs out of edges (neither occurs at the derived size); a full face buffer ends EPA with its closest face, as C's `epa`, instead of no contact. (2) `HFIELD_MARGIN_SHRINK` (default True; only with `HFIELD_PRISM_POLYTOPE`, as upstream keeps heightfields off its shrink): a heightfield prism pair with a margin or gap runs GJK on the uninflated shapes first and EPA only when they overlap, as MuJoCo C's `mjc_ccd` (upstream does it for non-heightfield pairs); before, every prism within margin + gap ran EPA on the inflated shapes. No effect at margin = gap = 0 (heightfield contact checks bitwise unchanged). rough_il3 smoke (4096 envs, 8 iterations, the 14-inch on AC, ratios only): `EPA_HORIZON` 3 worlds -> 0; per PPO iteration 2.05x the plane-path pin `8eb51fe` -> 1.68x; the 2.3.2 heightfield config unchanged (+0.3 %). `HFIELD_PRISM_POLYTOPE` and `HFIELD_MARGIN_SHRINK` are read by `wp.static` when `collision_gjk` is imported: change them in the source (assigning them after import has no effect). Tests: `test_box_box_horizon`, `test_epa_horizon_size`, `test_horizon_is_loop`, `test_epa_nonloop_horizon`, `test_hfield_mesh_gap_distance`. |
 
 Every flex change and every solver launch-form change is behind a module-level flag or environment variable that restores upstream's behaviour; the details and measurements are in
